/T (An Application Programming Interface \(API\) is a defined way for one piece of software to ask another piece of software to do something. It describes which operations exist, what input each operation needs, what output it returns, and which errors can happen. APIs exist at many levels: the functions of a code library, the system calls of an operating system, or the operations of a remote service. A web API is an API that is used through HTTP.)
/E (An Application Programming Interface \(API\) is a defined way for one piece of software to ask another piece of software to do something. It describes which operations exist, what input each operation needs, what output it returns, and which errors can happen. APIs exist at many levels: the functions of a code library, the system calls of an operating system, or the operations of a remote service. A web API is an API that is used through HTTP.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
