/T (GraphQL is a query language for APIs and a server-side runtime that executes queries against a type system defined by the service \(GraphQL Foundation, n.d.\). The client describes exactly which fields it needs, and the server returns exactly that shape. A GraphQL API usually exposes a single HTTP endpoint, and most requests are sent with POST.)
/E (GraphQL is a query language for APIs and a server-side runtime that executes queries against a type system defined by the service \(GraphQL Foundation, n.d.\). The client describes exactly which fields it needs, and the server returns exactly that shape. A GraphQL API usually exposes a single HTTP endpoint, and most requests are sent with POST.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
