/E (Limitations: the payload is encoded, not encrypted, so anyone who has the token can read it. Sensitive data must not be put inside. A token cannot be easily revoked before it expires, so access tokens should be short-lived. Implementations must verify the signature, the algorithm, and the expiry, as recommended in the JWT best current practices \(Sheffer et al., 2020\).)
