/E (A monolith is an application built and deployed as one unit. Its modules run in the same process and usually share one database. Microservices are an architecture style in which an application is built as a collection of small, autonomous services. Each service focuses on a single business capability and can be developed and deployed independently \(Microsoft, n.d.-b\).)
