/E (How it works: the server counts requests per client \(by API key, user, or IP address\). Common algorithms are fixed window, sliding window, and token bucket. When the limit is exceeded, the server answers 429 Too Many Requests, and it may include a Retry-After header that says how long the client should wait \(MDN Contributors, n.d.-a; Nottingham & Fielding, 2012\).)
