/T (Retries can fix temporary problems, but they can also cause damage. Microsoft's guidance for the Retry pattern is to retry only transient faults, to wait between attempts, to stop after a limited number of attempts, to log failures, and to consider whether the operation is idempotent. If it is not, a retry might execute it more than once \(Microsoft, n.d.-c\).)
/E (Retries can fix temporary problems, but they can also cause damage. Microsoft's guidance for the Retry pattern is to retry only transient faults, to wait between attempts, to stop after a limited number of attempts, to log failures, and to consider whether the operation is idempotent. If it is not, a retry might execute it more than once \(Microsoft, n.d.-c\).)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [2]
