/Title (A web service is a software system that offers data or functions to other programs over a network, using web technologies. A program sends a request, the service processes it, and the service sends back a response. No person needs to read a web page in the middle of this exchange.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 6091 0 R
/Next 6204 0 R
>>
endobj
6204 0 obj
<<
/Title (The term has a narrow and a broad meaning. In the original sense, "web services" meant services described with WSDL and exchanged with SOAP messages \(Chinnici et al., 2007\). Today the term is also used for any service reachable over HTTP, including REST APIs. In this document we use the broad meaning.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 6091 0 R
/Prev 6203 0 R
>>
