/Title (SOAP \(originally "Simple Object Access Protocol", but now just a name\) is a protocol for exchanging structured information between systems. It defines an extensible messaging framework, uses XML technologies, and can run over several underlying protocols \(Gudgin et al., 2007\). A SOAP message has an Envelope that contains an optional Header and a required Body. Errors are reported with a Fault element inside the Body. SOAP services are normally described with a WSDL file. Extensions such as WS- Security add features like message-level signing and encryption.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 6094 0 R
>>
endobj
