/Title (XML \(Extensible Markup Language\) is a markup language for structured documents, defined by the W3C \(Bray et al., 2008\). JSON \(JavaScript Object Notation\) is a lightweight, text-based format for data exchange \(Bray, 2017\).)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 6222 0 R
/Next 6237 0 R
>>
endobj
6237 0 obj
<<
/Title (Important: XML and JSON are data formats. They describe how data is written. They do not define how messages are sent, which operations exist, or how errors are handled. SOAP uses XML, while REST APIs most often use JSON, but a REST API could also return XML.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 6222 0 R
/Prev 6236 0 R
>>
endobj
