/Title (Purpose: protect data while it travels between client and server. HTTPS is HTTP carried over TLS, and it gives confidentiality, integrity, and server authentication \(Fielding et al., 2022; Rescorla, 2018\). How it works: the client and the server perform a TLS handshake, the server presents a certificate, and both sides create keys to encrypt the traffic. The https URL scheme tells the client to use TLS. Benefits: prevents eavesdropping and tampering on the network, and lets the client check that it is talking to the real server.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 6331 0 R
/Next 6357 0 R
>>
endobj
